    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a clear mandate: exploit vulnerable right-handed arms to rack up counting stats. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13) stands as our premier play, benefiting from a high-leverage matchup against Dobnak. The combination of an elite batting order spot (#1), a favorable SP_xERA of 5.16, and a wind-assisted venue makes him an absolute must-start. He is flanked in the \"Elite\" tier by **Trea Turner** (77.93) and **Kyle Schwarber** (77.21), both of whom benefit immensely from a plus-matchup against Bieber. Given that stolen bases are our scarcest category, **Trea Turner**\u2019s ability to leverage his speed against a pitcher with a 5.23 xERA makes him the engine of today's scoring projection.\n\nWe are forced to be disciplined at the margins, evidenced by our treatment of **Josh Smith** (33.53). Despite his utility, he falls well below our 40-point efficiency floor due to a brutal platoon disadvantage against Luzardo and a low-impact spot in the #8 hole. Consequently, the bench remains deep but static, as we monitor the lineup status for **Junior Caminero** (62.17) and **Lars Nootbaar** (48.47). While **Junior Caminero** remains a strong play in the #3 spot, we must watch for any late-breaking news regarding his availability. Similarly, **Yordan Alvarez** (68.54) remains a cornerstone of our lineup even without a confirmed opponent, as his xwOBA profile remains untouchable regardless of the day's specific pitcher.\n\nThe primary risk today involves managing our game caps while balancing platoon efficiencies. We have opted to favor **Colt Keith** (53.46) over internal options due to his sustained output, even though he faces the tricky Webb. Conversely, **Dillon Dingler** (40.41) and **Carson Benge** (44.69) are operating near our functional floor. Should the wind shift or late defensive shifts negate their platoon advantages, we are prepared to pivot to the high-upside potential of our bench, though we currently lack clear substitutes like **Christian Yelich**, **Caleb Durbin**, or **Chase Meidroth**, all of whom are currently out of their respective MLB rotations. We will continue to carry depth pieces like **Nelson Velazquez**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Pedro Ramirez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Jacob Gonzalez** as insurance against mid-game substitutions.",
